# MQL5 sources are UTF-16LE with a BOM, which is what MetaEditor writes and
# expects. Git treats UTF-16 as BINARY: without this, every change to a 3,952
# line .mq5 shows as "Bin 425948 -> 425960 bytes" with no diff, no blame and no
# merge. Measured, not assumed.
#
# working-tree-encoding stores UTF-8 in the repository — diffable, greppable,
# reviewable on GitHub — and converts back to UTF-16LE+BOM on checkout, so the
# files MetaEditor opens are byte-identical to what it wrote.
#
# Needs Git 2.18 or newer. On an older client the checkout is UTF-8 and
# MetaEditor will complain; that is the trade, and it is worth it.
*.mq5  working-tree-encoding=UTF-16LE-BOM text eol=crlf
*.mqh  working-tree-encoding=UTF-16LE-BOM text eol=crlf

# Presets are UTF-16LE+BOM too — verified, not assumed.
*.set  working-tree-encoding=UTF-16LE-BOM text eol=crlf

*.md   text eol=lf
*.php  text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf

# Compiled output is opaque either way.
*.ex5  binary
